# SABOTAGE: issue #11 / EG6 — the new `{:error, reason, usage}` arm in `dispatch/4` passes
# the adapter's REASON through raw instead of through `normalize_error/2`. "We now have
# structure, so the reason can travel" is exactly the regression the issue warned about:
# a rich reason (a tuple echoing the prompt) would reach the agent loop beside the usage.
#
# Flips the reason-normalized test. Every atom-reason test stays green (an atom passes the
# normalizer unchanged anyway), which is why the red needs a NON-atom reason.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/chokepoint_error_usage_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: EG6: the reason is still normalized — a rich reason never travels beside the usage
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/chokepoint.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/chokepoint.ex
index dfb4f1f..a5733e0 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/chokepoint.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/chokepoint.ex
@@ -379,7 +379,8 @@ defmodule Samen.AI.Chokepoint do
     # an allowlist, never the adapter's map. A non-map or a struct (an exception, say) in
     # the usage slot is not usage and falls to the catch-all below.
     {:error, reason, usage} when is_map(usage) and not is_struct(usage) ->
-      {:error, normalize_error(reason, provider), scrub_usage(usage)}
+      # SABOTAGE (#11 / EG6): the reason skips the normalizer on the usage arm.
+      {:error, reason, scrub_usage(usage)}
 
     other ->
       {:error, normalize_error(other, provider)}
